{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneMcKayValueMap","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneMcKayValueMap","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneStandardRepQDim"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_shape_311","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_shape_311","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneMcKayValueMap.lean#L67-L82","doc":"**Value map, A₅-split mark-6 node (electron block `(3,1,1)`): `[2]_q · d_q(3,1,1) = [3]_q·[4]_q`**\n(multiplicative, division-free). Hooks of the self-conjugate `(3,1,1)` are `{5,2,1,2,1}`, so\n\n  `[2]_q · [5]_q!  =  [3]_q · [4]_q · ([5]_q · [2]_q · [1]_q · [2]_q · [1]_q)`,\n\nthe last factor being the hook-length product; equivalently `d_q(3,1,1) = [5]_q!/∏hooks\n= [3]_q·[4]_q/[2]_q`. This is **not** `[6]_q`: the electron block is the McKay node where the\n`A₅` irrep `3⊕3′` (dim 6) splits, and the deviation of `d_q` from `[mark]_q = [6]_q` is exactly this\nsplit. Proved from the `qFactorial_succ` recursion, `[1]_q = 1`, and `ring`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_shape_32","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.qFactorial_shape_32","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneMcKayValueMap.lean#L51-L65","doc":"**Value map, mark-5 node (muon block `(3,2)`): `d_q(3,2) = [5]_q`** (multiplicative,\ndivision-free). Hooks of `(3,2)` are `{4,3,1,2,1}`, so\n\n  `[5]_q!  =  [5]_q · ([4]_q · [3]_q · [1]_q · [2]_q · [1]_q)`,\n\nthe parenthesized factor being the hook-length product; equivalently `d_q(3,2) = [5]_q!/∏hooks\n= [5]_q`. Proved from `[5]_q! = [5]_q·[4]_q!` and `[4]_q! = [4]_q·[3]_q·[2]_q·[1]_q` (`qFactorial_succ`\nrecursion), `[1]_q = 1`, and `ring`. This is the **new exact identity** of the McKay value map\n(#3685): the muon block value is the `q`-integer of its McKay Coxeter mark `5`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}